To learn more about &lt;a href="https://f.tomhjx.top/proxy/auto.clashx.yaml">Free ClashX Configuration Yaml&lt;/a></description></item><item><title>Network: IP Information</title><link>/network/ip-information/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/network/ip-information/</guid><description>
&lt;div class="container-fluid">
&lt;div class="input-group mb-3 row">
&lt;button class="btn btn-outline-primary form-control" type="button" id="query">Query&lt;/button>
&lt;input type="text" class="form-control w-75" id="ipInput" placeholder="IPv4/IPv6" aria-describedby="query" />
&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="mb-3 row">
&lt;table class="table table-info table-hover table-bordered table-striped-columns">
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">IP&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ip">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Latitude&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipLatitude">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Longitude&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipLongitude">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Time Zone&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipTZ">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Country Code&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipCC">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Country&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipC">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Region&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipRegion">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Region Code&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipRegionCode">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">City&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipCity">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Postal Code&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipPC">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">Organization&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipOrganization">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">ASN&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipAsn">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">ASN Organization&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipAsnOrganization">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th scope="row">ISP&lt;/th>
&lt;td id="ipISP">&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>
&lt;script>
$(function(){
$('#query').click(function(){
ip = $('#ipInput').val();
$.getJSON("https://api.ip.sb/geoip/"+encodeURIComponent(ip),
function(d) {
$('#ip').text(d.ip);
$('#ipOrganization').text(d.organization);
$('#ipAsn').text(d.asn);
$('#ipAsnOrganization').text(d.asn_organization);
$('#ipTZ').text(d.timezone);
$('#ipCC').text(d.country_code);
$('#ipC').text(d.country);
$('#ipRegion').text(d.region);
$('#ipRegionCode').text(d.region_code);
$('#ipCity').text(d.city);
$('#ipPC').text(d.postal_code);
$('#ipLatitude').text(d.latitude);
$('#ipLongitude').text(d.longitude);
$('#ipISP').text(d.isp);
}
);
});
});
&lt;/script></description></item><item><title>Network: Network Speed Test</title><link>/network/speed-test/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/network/speed-test/</guid><description>
&lt;div id="speed-test" class="container-fluid px-0">
&lt;p class="lead">Find out how fast your internet connection is.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Test provider: Cloudflare. The test connects to this third-party service only after you click Start test, and the provider can see your IP address. Each test downloads about 20 MB and uploads about 5 MB, plus a small amount of protocol overhead. Tests run for up to 90 seconds and can be stopped at any time.&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="row">
&lt;div class="col-6 col-lg-3 mb-3">&lt;div class="speed-metric">&lt;h2>Download&lt;/h2>&lt;div>&lt;strong id="speed-download">—&lt;/strong> &lt;span>Mbps&lt;/span>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="col-6 col-lg-3 mb-3">&lt;div class="speed-metric">&lt;h2>Upload&lt;/h2>&lt;div>&lt;strong id="speed-upload">—&lt;/strong> &lt;span>Mbps&lt;/span>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="col-6 col-lg-3 mb-3">&lt;div class="speed-metric">&lt;h2>HTTP latency&lt;/h2>&lt;div>&lt;strong id="speed-latency">—&lt;/strong> &lt;span>ms&lt;/span>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="col-6 col-lg-3 mb-3">&lt;div class="speed-metric">&lt;h2>Jitter&lt;/h2>&lt;div>&lt;strong id="speed-jitter">—&lt;/strong> &lt;span>ms&lt;/span>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="mb-3">
&lt;button id="speed-start" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Start test&lt;/button>
&lt;button id="speed-stop" class="btn btn-outline-secondary ml-2" type="button" disabled>Stop&lt;/button>
&lt;/div>
&lt;progress id="speed-progress" max="10" value="0" aria-label="Speed test progress" style="width:100%">&lt;/progress>
&lt;p id="speed-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="mt-2">Ready. Click Start test to begin.&lt;/p>
&lt;details class="mt-4">
&lt;summary>Understanding your results&lt;/summary>
&lt;ul class="mt-3">
&lt;li>Mbps means megabits per second. Divide by 8 to convert to MB/s. Download and upload tests transfer fixed amounts of data over a single connection and include request round-trip time.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>HTTP latency is the average round-trip time of 5 requests after a warm-up request. It includes server processing time and is not ICMP ping. Jitter is the average absolute difference between consecutive latency samples.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Results reflect the connection from your browser to Cloudflare and depend on Wi-Fi, proxies, background traffic, and server location. Short samples may underestimate fast connections and do not represent your internet provider's maximum bandwidth.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>If the connection fails, check your network, proxy, or browser blocking settings and try again. Results from completed stages are kept; unfinished measurements show “—”.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;/details>
&lt;noscript>&lt;p class="alert alert-warning">Enable JavaScript to use the network speed test.&lt;/p>&lt;/noscript>
&lt;/div>
&lt;style>
#speed-test .speed-metric { height: 100%; padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid #dce4e8; border-top: 3px solid #30638e; border-radius: .25rem; background: #f6f9fb; color: #233746; }
#speed-test .speed-metric h2 { font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
#speed-test .speed-metric strong { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
#speed-test .speed-metric span { font-size: .85rem; }
#speed-test summary { cursor: pointer; }
&lt;/style>
&lt;script src="/js/speed-test.js" defer>&lt;/script></description></item></channel></rss>